		{"kind": "arena", "style": "titan", "id": "world.greywood.rootwarden_territory", "pos": [-790, 200], "inner_radius": 110, "engage_area": "world.area.rootwarden_grove", "engage": {"at": [-790, 196], "size": [52, 30, 52], "yaw": 0}, "boss_id": "world.greywood.rootwarden", "encounter_id": "encounter.greywood_rootwarden", "defeated_flag": "boss.rootwarden.defeated", "territory_m": 95, "region_id": "region.greywood", "discover_poi": "poi.rootwarden_grove", "reopened_flag": "world.greywood.grove_greened", "disengage_s": 6, "disengage_margin_m": 20, "wake_on_sight": false, "wake_flag": "world.rootwarden.called", "note": "B3: the Rootwarden's territory (TitanTerritory). He sleeps rooted in his grove: a giant he sees only discovers the grove (no fight); a blow wakes him at any time, and once the woodfolk call the giant to lay him to rest (world.rootwarden.called) entering the hollow's floor wakes him too. Rooted until his second phase, he hunts only when uprooted, never beyond 130 m of the grove (the old root ride, 100 m off, is the edge of his reach; he never comes out onto the rides). Once he is at rest and the giant has gone on, the grove greens (world.greywood.grove_greened)."},
		{"kind": "grove", "style": "trunk", "id": "world.greywood.rootwarden_trunks", "pos": [-790, 200], "points": [[-734.4, 204.9], [-748.2, 226.1], [-762.9, 245.1], [-786.3, 253.4], [-809.0, 244.8], [-832.9, 236.0], [-837.3, 210.9], [-842.2, 187.0], [-835.3, 162.2], [-812.9, 143.2], [-783.8, 139.6], [-762.7, 151.4]], "size": [6.5, 46], "poi": "poi.rootwarden_grove", "landmark": true, "skyline": true, "note": "B3: the ring of colossal trees round the warden's hollow (the grove's landmark over the wood). B5: the four south of his spot stand 46-48 m from him (they stood 34-43 m off, within a step of his root-lash's 25 m: a giant out of its reach on that side was against their trunks)."},
		{"kind": "grove", "style": "root_arch", "id": "world.greywood.rootwarden_arch", "pos": [-750, 172], "yaw": -49, "size": [30, 26, 2.8], "note": "B3: a root grown up out of the ground and back into it, arched over the warden ride's end: the way into his hollow."},
